{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender UI Button.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender UI Button.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender ui button blender ui button","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender UI Button.md","fileName":"Blender UI Button.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender UI Button","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:20\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Editor Construction]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Editor Construction","Blender UI Block","Blender Editor Button Operator Binding","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender UI Button.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender UI Button.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender ui button blender ui button","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender UI Button.md","fileName":"Blender UI Button.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender UI Button","heading":"Blender UI Button","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A core Blender UI button is created through the interface API with a control type, identifier, label, location, dimensions, optional data pointer, numeric bounds, auxiliary values, and tooltip. The returned runtime object belongs to a [[Blender UI Block]] that coordinates the surrounding controls.\n\nIn the tutorial editor, the button does not keep an independent value; its purpose is to invoke an operation that changes the main region. [[Blender Editor Button Operator Binding]] stores the corresponding operator type so an ordinary interface event reaches the correct poll and execution callbacks.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Editor Construction","Blender UI Block","Blender Editor Button Operator Binding","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Ful